      "text": "To find the maximum value of the expression \\(\\frac{(x + y)^2}{x^2 + y^2}\\), we start by expanding the numerator:\n\n\\[\n(x + y)^2 = x^2 + 2xy + y^2.\n\\]\n\nThus, the expression becomes:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{x^2 + 2xy + y^2}{x^2 + y^2}.\n\\]\n\nWe can split this fraction into three separate fractions:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{x^2}{x^2 + y^2} + \\frac{2xy}{x^2 + y^2} + \\frac{y^2}{x^2 + y^2}.\n\\]\n\nNext, we analyze each of these terms separately. First, consider the term \\(\\frac{x^2}{x^2 + y^2}\\). Since \\(x^2 + y^2 \\geq 2xy\\) by the AM-GM inequality, we have:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{x^2}{x^2 + y^2} \\leq \\frac{x^2}{2xy} = \\frac{x}{2y}.\n\\]\n\nSimilarly, for the term \\(\\frac{y^2}{x^2 + y^2}\\), we have:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{y^2}{x^2 + y^2} \\leq \\frac{y^2}{2xy} = \\frac{y}{2x}.\n\\]\n\nNow, consider the term \\(\\frac{2xy}{x^2 + y^2}\\). We need to maximize this term. Notice that:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{2xy}{x^2 + y^2} \\leq \\frac{2xy}{2xy} = 1.\n\\]\n\nTo find a specific value that might achieve the maximum, we test if \\(x = y\\). If \\(x = y\\), then the expression becomes:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{(x + x)^2}{x^2 + x^2} = \\frac{(2x)^2}{2x^2} = \\frac{4x^2}{2x^2} = 2.\n\\]\n\nThus, the maximum value of \\(\\frac{(x + y)^2}{x^2 + y^2}\\) is \\(\\boxed{2}\\).",
