      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To find the maximum value of \\(\\frac{(x + y)^2}{x^2 + y^2}\\), we start by expanding the numerator:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{(x + y)^2}{x^2 + y^2} = \\frac{x^2 + 2xy + y^2}{x^2 + y^2}.\n\\]\n\nWe can separate this fraction into three parts:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{x^2 + 2xy + y^2}{x^2 + y^2} = \\frac{x^2}{x^2 + y^2} + \\frac{2xy}{x^2 + y^2} + \\frac{y^2}{x^2 + y^2}.\n\\]\n\nNext, we simplify each term individually. First, consider \\(\\frac{x^2}{x^2 + y^2}\\):\n\n\\[\n\\frac{x^2}{x^2 + y^2} = 1 - \\frac{y^2}{x^2 + y^2}.\n\\]\n\nSimilarly, consider \\(\\frac{y^2}{x^2 + y^2}\\):\n\n\\[\n\\frac{y^2}{x^2 + y^2} = 1 - \\frac{x^2}{x^2 + y^2}.\n\\]\n\nThus, the expression becomes:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{x^2}{x^2 + y^2} + \\frac{2xy}{x^2 + y^2} + \\frac{y^2}{x^2 + y^2} = \\frac{1}{x^2 + y^2} \\left( x^2 + 2xy + y^2 \\right) = \\frac{(x + y)^2}{x^2 + y^2}.\n\\]\n\nTo find the maximum value, we need to determine the behavior of this expression. Notice that:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{(x + y)^2}{x^2 + y^2} \\leq x^2 + y^2.\n\\]\n\nThis is true because:\n\n\\[\n(x + y)^2 = x^2 + 2xy + y^2 \\leq x^2 + y^2 + 2xy = (x^2 + y^2 + 2xy - 2xy) \\leq (x^2 + y^2) + 2xy \\leq x^2 + y^2 + 2xy = (x^2 + y^2 + 2xy - 2xy) \\leq (x^2 + y^2).\n\\]\n\nThus, the maximum value is achieved when \\(x = y\\). Substituting \\(x = y\\) into the expression, we get:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{(x + x)^2}{x^2 + x^2} = \\frac{(2x)^2}{2x^2} = \\frac{4x^2}{2x^2} = 2.\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the maximum value of \\(\\frac{(x + y)^2}{x^2 + y^2}\\) is \\(\\boxed{2}\\).",
